  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math><msub><mrow><mi>z</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi>z</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> be two complex numbers satisfying <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>|</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>|</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn></math> and <math><mo>|</mo><msub><mrow><mi>z</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>i</mi><mo>|</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math>. Then the minimum value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math> is :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>2</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>0</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>We have,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>:</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>:</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0146_a1561460fbc1.png\" style=\"width: 203px; height: 200px;\" /></p><p>Centres of the circles are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#8801;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#8801;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>.</p><p>Radius of the circles are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><msup><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>4</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p><p>Circles touch each other internally.<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> at the point of contact.</p></blockquote>"
  }
}